{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01481",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 10.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.72,
      "end_seconds": 15.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.26,
      "end_seconds": 22.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "Doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.39,
      "end_seconds": 31.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "It's swelling in both ankles. I thought I'd wait, but it it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 33.07,
      "end_seconds": 42.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier temperature is 37.0 degrees, saturation 89 percent, pulse is 93 beats a minute blood pressure 121 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.38,
      "end_seconds": 48.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Okay, when did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.76,
      "end_seconds": 52.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "it's been going on for about a month"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.7,
      "end_seconds": 61.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.07,
      "end_seconds": 75.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say. Only raising the legs, and it's not much. It's every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.82,
      "end_seconds": 80.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Alright, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.07,
      "end_seconds": 85.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "It usually comes with breathlessness when I lie flat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.52,
      "end_seconds": 94.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.01,
      "end_seconds": 102.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say it happens once or twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.47,
      "end_seconds": 109.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "a few quick ones: fever, coughing up blood or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.21,
      "end_seconds": 125.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.48,
      "text": "No, no fever, no coughing up blood, no chest pain. I was waking up at night short of breath at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.55,
      "end_seconds": 132.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any calf pain, fainting or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.24,
      "end_seconds": 137.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "No, nothing to to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.86,
      "end_seconds": 140.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.16,
      "end_seconds": 143.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.88,
      "end_seconds": 147.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.29,
      "end_seconds": 152.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "No, um, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 153.51,
      "end_seconds": 161.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "Actually, I remember he had some kind of reaction to trimethoprim before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.54,
      "end_seconds": 166.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.4,
      "end_seconds": 173.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.68,
      "end_seconds": 182.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called it's a small white one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.62,
      "end_seconds": 188.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.41,
      "end_seconds": 212.58,
      "duration_seconds": 23.17,
      "text": "For my heart, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Valsartan. I take it 80 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure. I used to take metoprolol, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.22,
      "end_seconds": 218.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.59,
      "end_seconds": 223.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Heart failure, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.56,
      "end_seconds": 225.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.37,
      "end_seconds": 234.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for two years now. I've had heart disease, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.54,
      "end_seconds": 243.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Right, so high blood pressure is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.23,
      "end_seconds": 257.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "right, have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.36,
      "end_seconds": 264.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Yes, I had part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.95,
      "end_seconds": 283.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.18,
      "end_seconds": 290.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "My sister had breast cancer. My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.97,
      "end_seconds": 294.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "okay, a few questions about your lifestyle now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.68,
      "end_seconds": 312.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.51,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. No, I've never smoked in my life. I walk the dog every morning. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.98,
      "end_seconds": 317.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.53,
      "end_seconds": 320.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.34,
      "end_seconds": 331.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Neck veins are raised."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.75,
      "end_seconds": 336.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.66,
      "end_seconds": 356.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "There's pitting oedema up to the shins on both legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.92,
      "end_seconds": 359.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.6,
      "end_seconds": 362.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.14,
      "end_seconds": 378.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "I can hear crackles at the bases of both lungs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.0,
      "end_seconds": 401.47,
      "duration_seconds": 17.47,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again from what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with fluid overload related to the heart i'd also keep a kidney problem in mind we shouldn't forget a chest infection"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 402.11,
      "end_seconds": 406.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "I've already done an ECG, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.8,
      "end_seconds": 414.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "Okay, I'll take a look at that. I want blood tests done, that's for heart failure review."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 416.15,
      "end_seconds": 418.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "How long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.51,
      "end_seconds": 445.67,
      "duration_seconds": 26.16,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an echocardiogram because of breathlessness and swelling. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Keep the salt and the fluids moderate, no more than about one and a half litres a day. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 446.27,
      "end_seconds": 451.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Sure. I'd like to see you again after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 453.05,
      "end_seconds": 454.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Yes, that's manageable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.23,
      "end_seconds": 459.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.71,
      "end_seconds": 465.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Hmm, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.31,
      "end_seconds": 467.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}